sistent with daytime outdoor activity.\n\n---\n\n**4) Signs of poor maintenance/dilapidation: ✅**\n\n- The ground is mostly dirt and patchy grass, not paved or landscaped (frames 616, 623, 631, 643).\n- Paint on rides is faded or peeling (e.g., the swing ride base in frame 623, carousel in 643).\n- The fence around the swing ride is mismatched and rusted (frames 618, 631).\n- The pavement is cracked and uneven (frames 636, 645).\n\n---\n\n**5) Rusty or broken equipment/rides: ✅**\n\n- The swing ride’s chains and structure show signs of rust and wear (frames 616, 621, 633).\n- The carousel ride (frame 643) appears outdated and neglected — seats are empty, paint is faded, and surrounding area is unkempt.\n- No active maintenance or staff visible; rides appear to be operating with minimal oversight.\n\n---\n\n**6) Overgrown vegetation or neglect: ✅**\n\n- Grass is patchy and dry (frames 616, 623, 643).\n- Weeds and unkempt bushes are visible around ride bases and fences (frames 618, 631, 644).\n- Trees and shrubs encroach on walkways and ride areas, suggesting lack of landscaping or upkeep.\n\n---\n\n**Temporal Context:**\n\n- These frames (616–645) are consistent with a single location and time period — the afternoon visit to the amusement park.\n- The sequence shows the team arriving, riding attractions, and walking around — no indication these are from different scenes (e.g., frames 240–247 or 574–649 are not included here and are irrelevant to this analysis).\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nCompared to most modern, well-maintained amusement parks (which typically feature clean pavements, bright paint, manicured lawns, and modern safety features), this park exhibits clear signs of neglect, aging infrastructure, and minimal upkeep. The visual evidence strongly supports the classification **‘0’ (Not well maintained)**.\n\n✅ **Answer: 0 is correct.**'}, {'batch_start': 90, 'batch_end': 94, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/_T2Avd3tFHc/frames/frame_06